  "question": {
    "text": "The diffraction pattern of a light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi>nm</mi></math> diffracting from a slit of width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mm</mi></math> is focused on the focal plane of a convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The width of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st </mtext></msup></math> secondary maxima will be :"
  },
